# Vendored XCFrameworks from the sparrow-domain, sparrow-cold-storage and
# sparrow-kit releases. ~34 MB, and they change wholesale on every release —
# exactly what Git is worst at storing.
#
# ⚠️ Everything under Frameworks/ is tracked, not just the Mach-O binaries. The
# executables inside a .framework have no extension, so a pattern that tried to
# match by suffix would miss precisely the large files. A few small text files
# (Info.plist, .swiftinterface) go to LFS as collateral; that is the cheaper
# mistake.
#
# ⚠️ A clone without git-lfs installed gets 130-byte pointer files that Xcode
# will try to link, failing with an unhelpful "not a valid Mach-O". Run
# `git lfs install` before the first clone.
Frameworks/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
